        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "STRUCTURES IT CLAUSE ADVERBIAL CLAUSE 1 Subject + Verb + It + Adverbial Clause I hate it She loves it I don’t mind it when someone runs late all the time. when the kids play quietly. when someone laughs out loud. 2 It + Verb + Noun + Adverbial clause It upsets me It bothers my dad when my mums shouts for no reason. when my little brother is noisy. There are some other phrases that may be considered adverbial clauses as well. Condition: if / Unless / As if / Only if - You’ll get permission only if your father agrees. Place: Everywhere / Wherever / Anywhere - Wherever I go, I see her. Reason: Now that / Because / Since - You can start painting the room now that your brother is gone.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "STRUCTURES IT CLAUSE ADVERBIAL CLAUSE 1 Subject + Verb + It + Adverbial Clause I hate it She loves it I don’t mind it when someone runs late all the time. when the kids play quietly. when someone laughs out loud. 2 It + Verb + Noun + Adverbial clause It upsets me It bothers my dad when my mums shouts for no reason. when my little brother is noisy. There are some other phrases that may be considered adverbial clauses as well. Condition: if / Unless / As if / Only if - You’ll get permission only if your father agrees. Place: Everywhere / Wherever / Anywhere - Wherever I go, I see her. Reason: Now that / Because / Since - You can start painting the room now that your brother is gone.",
          "Among the ways we can express perspectives, we can consider the following structures."
